@Steven M.

The bridge grand slam requires, first, that a player contract to take all 13 tricks and, second, successfully do so.  If you contract to take 12 tricks and wind up taking all 13, for example, that is merely a small slam with an overtrick.

You get a lot more points for a grand slam, but they are rarely bid, because it is seldom that you are confident about being able to take all 13 tricks, and making a small slam (with or without an overtrick) still scores very well.

